WEBVTT

00:00:03.333 --> 00:00:04.333
[sighs]

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.833
Dad.

00:00:06.916 --> 00:00:10.208
Fur from whoever's helping
the bunny and the snake.

00:00:12.791 --> 00:00:14.750
Find Pawbert.

00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:19.000
[Pawbert]
Almost to me hideout.

00:00:19.083 --> 00:00:20.375
[chuckles]

00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:21.541
Snake in the hole.

00:00:21.625 --> 00:00:22.458
Ooh. Yeah, yeah.

00:00:22.541 --> 00:00:23.541
[Judy] Oh!

00:00:24.666 --> 00:00:25.500
Oh!

00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:27.958
We shall succeed, Judy Hopps.

00:00:28.041 --> 00:00:31.416
We'll stop the Lynxleys
and save your partner.

00:00:31.916 --> 00:00:34.041
I'm sorry. You are...

00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:36.625
Oh. Gary. Gary the Snake.

00:00:36.708 --> 00:00:38.166
And your last name?

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.500
De'Snake.

00:00:39.583 --> 00:00:42.041
Everything is gonna be okay.

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:44.291
[gagging]

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.250
[clears throat]

00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:49.791
[chuckles nervously]

00:00:50.708 --> 00:00:54.416
[Gary chuckles] Teaming up
with you is very exciting.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.500
Ooh! Uh,
don't worry about my fang.

00:00:57.583 --> 00:01:00.083
I got my own anti-venom pen.

00:01:00.166 --> 00:01:01.458
Stops the toxin.

00:01:01.541 --> 00:01:03.750
[anti-venom pen]
Stab me
straight into the heart.

00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:04.750
[Judy chuckles nervously]

00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:06.750
[chuckles, gasps]

00:01:08.166 --> 00:01:10.958
Welcome to my oasis...
[chuckles]

00:01:11.041 --> 00:01:13.000
...away from my evil family.

00:01:13.083 --> 00:01:15.541
I like to come here,
just kind of veg out.

00:01:15.625 --> 00:01:16.916
Ooh!

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.083
-Get with all my cat stuff.
-Wow.

00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:21.666
-No! That's actually vintage.
-Awesome.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.416
[chuckles] No!
If you could just not.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.166
-[Gary] Ooh!
-No! No, please don't.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.083
-Wow!
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:26.166 --> 00:01:27.833
-Mammals get the best stuff.
-No.

00:01:27.916 --> 00:01:29.333
-What's this do?
-Wait, not that.

00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:31.208
[purring]

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.500
Turn it off. Turn it off.
Turn it off. Turn it off.

00:01:33.583 --> 00:01:34.583
[clears throat]

00:01:35.166 --> 00:01:38.583
So, we should probably
get to the journal, hmm?

00:01:39.125 --> 00:01:42.083
How did you become partners?

00:01:42.166 --> 00:01:44.125
Oh, when I found out
the journal

00:01:44.208 --> 00:01:46.125
was going to be
on display at the Gala,

00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:49.708
I sent his family an anonymous
letter asking to see it.

00:01:49.791 --> 00:01:52.875
Luckily, they make Pawbert
work in the mail room,

00:01:52.958 --> 00:01:54.958
so he read it first.

00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:57.583
I got him smuggled in
from overseas.

00:01:57.666 --> 00:01:59.833
Seven days in a crate.

00:01:59.916 --> 00:02:03.416
But if I fix things for
my family, it'll be worth it.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.750
Then we'll fix things
for your partner too.

00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:08.958
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.833
Hey.

00:02:12.916 --> 00:02:15.875
I know coming with us
was hard,

00:02:16.833 --> 00:02:19.041
but we're gonna
help your partner,

00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:21.500
the same way
we're gonna help the city.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.666
We stop my family
and show everyone the truth.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.875
Are you ready?

00:02:28.958 --> 00:02:30.833
Light the fire.

00:02:40.125 --> 00:02:43.125
How much do you know?

00:02:43.208 --> 00:02:47.041
Well, uh, that his family
was framed,

00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:49.833
and there's some secret
hidden in the metal cover

00:02:49.916 --> 00:02:52.458
that only a snake can see.

00:02:53.125 --> 00:02:58.166
Not just any snake,
a heat-sensing pit viper.

00:02:59.166 --> 00:03:02.083
All it takes
is a little warmth.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:06.416
I just... I don't understand.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.541
Why would
your great-grandfather

00:03:08.625 --> 00:03:10.708
hide a secret for a snake?

00:03:10.791 --> 00:03:13.125
He didn't.

00:03:13.875 --> 00:03:14.875
I...

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.583
[gasps]

00:03:17.708 --> 00:03:19.708
It wasn't his journal.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.000
That's the secret.

00:03:23.833 --> 00:03:26.958
Zootropolis wasn't created
by a mammal.

00:03:27.875 --> 00:03:31.458
It was created by a snake.

00:03:31.541 --> 00:03:33.750
[Pawbert]
Gary's great-grandmother.

00:03:35.958 --> 00:03:37.541
She wanted to make the city
a place

00:03:37.625 --> 00:03:40.250
where all animals
felt welcome.

00:03:42.666 --> 00:03:45.458
So she invented
her weather walls

00:03:45.541 --> 00:03:47.750
to help everyone.

00:03:53.125 --> 00:03:54.291
ORIGINAL PATENT
Granted To Agnes De'Snake

00:03:54.375 --> 00:03:55.375
She just needed an investor.

00:03:56.541 --> 00:03:57.791
A partner.

00:03:59.458 --> 00:04:01.541
But when my great-grandfather

00:04:01.625 --> 00:04:03.958
saw what her idea
could be worth...

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.208
he plotted to steal her plans
for himself.

00:04:09.291 --> 00:04:11.291
ORIGINAL PATENT
Granted To Ebenezer Lynxley

00:04:17.916 --> 00:04:19.958
So he committed a murder...

00:04:22.291 --> 00:04:24.500
his own maid...

00:04:27.041 --> 00:04:29.333
and framed
Gary's great-grandmother.

00:04:29.416 --> 00:04:31.041
[clamoring]

00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:32.416
And because she was a snake...

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.041
MAMMALS AND REPTILES:
TOO DIFFERENT FOR ONE CITY?

00:04:34.125 --> 00:04:36.000
...everyone believed his lie.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:42.583
Soon, no reptiles
were welcome.

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.291
And over time,

00:04:45.375 --> 00:04:46.833
my great-grandfather

00:04:46.916 --> 00:04:52.125
buried the reptile
neighborhood in snow.

00:04:55.166 --> 00:05:00.750
And he died believing no one
could ever uncover his crimes.

00:05:01.791 --> 00:05:02.875
But...

00:05:04.708 --> 00:05:08.166
he was wrong.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.583
ORIGINAL PATENT
Granted To Agnes De'Snake

00:05:09.666 --> 00:05:13.125
[Judy]
Her original patent was saved.

00:05:14.375 --> 00:05:16.125
That's what
you're looking for.

00:05:16.208 --> 00:05:17.916
She hid it in her home.

00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:22.541
Find her home,
find her patent.

00:05:31.208 --> 00:05:34.208
We just didn't know
where her home was buried

00:05:35.375 --> 00:05:37.750
until now.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:41.083
[Pawbert] My family's land?

00:05:41.166 --> 00:05:46.250
But under all that snow,
how are we gonna find it?

00:05:46.833 --> 00:05:47.833
Wait.

00:05:47.916 --> 00:05:49.333
Clock tower.

00:05:49.416 --> 00:05:51.625
Her neighborhood,
the reptile neighborhood,

00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:52.875
had a clock tower.

00:05:52.958 --> 00:05:54.625
It lights up like a beacon.

00:05:54.708 --> 00:05:58.125
If it wasn't fully buried,
maybe we could see it.

00:05:58.208 --> 00:05:59.750
Follow it to her home.

00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:01.791
Except my great-grandfather
turned off the power.

00:06:01.875 --> 00:06:03.375
But we have the plans

00:06:03.458 --> 00:06:05.250
that show us
how to turn it back on.

00:06:05.333 --> 00:06:07.291
Oh! Ooh! Hmm.

00:06:07.375 --> 00:06:09.791
The power switch
to her whole neighborhood

00:06:09.875 --> 00:06:12.583
was in the original
control room.

00:06:12.666 --> 00:06:15.208
All right! And where is that?

00:06:15.291 --> 00:06:17.000
Inside the oldest wall
of the city.

00:06:17.083 --> 00:06:19.458
The Desert Tundratown
weather wall.

00:06:19.541 --> 00:06:22.583
We get inside,
turn on that switch,

00:06:22.666 --> 00:06:24.125
light the clock tower,

00:06:24.208 --> 00:06:28.166
-we find her house.
-We find her patent.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:31.000
And my family
is finally coming home.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.666
We will succeed, Judy Hopps.

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:36.625
We shall succeed!

00:06:38.791 --> 00:06:40.208
[Kitty gasps] I found him.

00:06:42.083 --> 00:06:43.541
Get me Hoggbottom.

00:06:43.625 --> 00:06:45.166
[alarm buzzes]

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.291
[groans]

00:06:46.375 --> 00:06:51.375
Ooh! It's Nicholas Wilde.
Big-time cop, huh?

00:06:51.458 --> 00:06:53.500
I'll see you
at the lunch table.

00:06:54.083 --> 00:06:56.625
I'm gonna tie your tail
in a knot.

00:06:56.708 --> 00:06:57.583
Hoggbottom--

00:06:57.666 --> 00:06:59.708
What are you looking at,
butthead?

00:06:59.791 --> 00:07:02.583
This is a mistake.
It's a setup. It's the lynxes.

00:07:02.666 --> 00:07:04.208
Listen to me. Please.

00:07:04.291 --> 00:07:07.083
I know we have had
our differences, right?

00:07:07.166 --> 00:07:09.875
But I've always
respected you--

00:07:10.708 --> 00:07:13.291
You don't respect anyone.

00:07:13.375 --> 00:07:15.166
[grunting]

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.625
Phone. It's Milton Lynxley.

00:07:17.708 --> 00:07:19.791
He's got
the rabbit's location.

00:07:19.875 --> 00:07:22.291
Whatever he says,
it's a lie, Hoggbottom.

00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:23.958
Hoggbottom, listen to me!

00:07:24.041 --> 00:07:25.083
Oh, God.

00:07:25.166 --> 00:07:27.375
[grunting]

00:07:27.458 --> 00:07:32.041
[Nibbles] Nicholas Wilde!

